In the family living room on an autumn afternoon, all four family members lift the finished cardboard rocket off the deep red rug together. The cardboard rocket stands as a tall cylinder of white-painted brown corrugated cardboard with a pointed nose cone at the top, three triangular red fins at its base, and a single round window in the front side of the body, with a shoebox airlock attached to its side, both flat brown lids closed tight on the box. Daniel, an adult man with short tousled dark brown wavy hair, a short beard and mustache, and brown eyes, wears a green knitted wool jumper, blue denim jeans, and brown leather boots, bending down and gripping the rocket's cylinder with both hands. Sarah, an adult woman with straight chin-length blonde hair parted at the side, rectangular dark-framed glasses, and blue eyes, wearing a purple long-sleeve cotton blouse, a grey wool skirt, a yellow knitted scarf, small grey drop earrings, and black ankle boots, holds the rocket's opposite side. Noah, a young school-age boy with tousled ear-length wavy light blonde hair, bangs below his eyebrows, and blue eyes, wears an orange fabric astronaut coverall with a grey webbing belt, a white quilted chest pack, and grey space boots, his fingers wrapped firmly around one red base fin. Emma, a preschool-age girl with wavy brown hair tied in a mid-back ponytail, brown eyes, freckles, and small stud earrings, wears a white fabric astronaut flight suit with a blue quilted puffer vest over it, a red utility belt, and chunky white space boots, her hands bracing the bottom edge of the rocket. Wide shot showing the honey-brown wooden floorboards, a grey sofa to the left, a tall wooden shelf unit against the right wall holding books, jars, and a large turnip lantern, and the closed glass balcony door in the far cream wall showing autumn foliage beyond.

