On the balcony floor beside the open door in the evening, Emma closes both of her hands around the tiny glowing creature nestled inside the open cardboard shoebox airlock. Emma, a preschool-age girl with wavy brown hair in a mid-back ponytail, brown eyes, freckles, and small stud earrings, wearing a white fabric astronaut flight suit, a blue quilted puffer vest, a red utility belt, and chunky white space boots, crouches on the grey concrete boards with her fingers curved gently around Funkel, a palm-sized winged creature glowing with soft warm gold light from its cream and pale-gold body, its large dark round eyes looking up happily. Noah, a young school-age boy with tousled ear-length light blonde hair, bangs below his eyebrows, and blue eyes, wearing an orange fabric astronaut coverall with a grey webbing belt, a white quilted chest pack, and grey space boots, leans in close on his knees with both palms pressed against the open upper rim of the rectangular brown shoebox airlock, watching with wide cheerful eyes. Close-up shot showing the grey concrete balcony boards scattered with fallen russet autumn leaves, the base of the white railing, and the side of the white-painted cardboard rocket rising beside them.

---METADATA---
