Inside the rocket cabin, Noah leans forward in anger and lunges for the turnip lantern, while Emma clutches it tightly against her chest, crying out in protest. Noah, seen over the shoulder with the back of his tousled light blonde head, neck, and orange coverall shoulder filling the foreground corner, extends his arm forward toward the lantern. Emma, a preschool-age girl with wavy brown hair in a ponytail, brown eyes, freckles, and small stud earrings, wearing a white fabric astronaut flight suit, a blue quilted puffer vest, and a red utility belt, stands backed against the white cardboard wall, both arms wrapped securely around her small carved turnip lantern, which glows with warm orange light through its triangular openings, her brows drawn up in sadness, mouth open crying out. Beyond the dark glass of the round forward window, the loose row of small lamps appears small and faint in the dark space outside. Over-the-shoulder shot focused across the small distance between the two children inside the white and red trimmed cabin.

---METADATA---
