Inside the rocket cabin, Emma pushes her small carved turnip lantern into the open outer end of the shoebox airlock, looking steadily through the round forward window toward Krax outside. Emma, a preschool-age girl with wavy brown hair in a mid-back ponytail, brown eyes, freckles, and small stud earrings, wearing a white fabric astronaut flight suit, a blue quilted puffer vest, and a red utility belt, stands waist-up at the brown shoebox airlock, guiding the glowing pale turnip lantern across the cardboard opening with both hands, warm orange light spilling from its cut triangular vents onto her fingers. The inner lid of the airlock remains shut across the top while the outer lid is open. Close-up shot showing the white painted cardboard wall, red trim, control levers, and the round window framing the silver feathers of Krax's star magpie nest outside in the dark dust.

---METADATA---
