On the residential balcony at dusk, all four family members step together out into the autumn air under an open evening sky. Noah, a young school-age boy with tousled ear-length light blonde hair, bangs below his eyebrows, and blue eyes, wearing an orange fabric astronaut coverall with a grey webbing belt, a white quilted chest pack, and grey space boots, holds his large carved turnip lantern aloft by its wire handle, its warm orange light glowing through cut openings and shining over the group. Emma, a preschool-age girl with wavy brown hair in a mid-back ponytail, brown eyes, freckles, and small stud earrings, wearing a white astronaut suit, blue puffer vest, red utility belt, and white space boots, stands beside him looking up happily toward a lone bright star blinking twice in the purple-blue twilight sky above. Daniel, an adult man with dark brown wavy hair, a short beard, and brown eyes, wearing a green wool jumper, blue jeans, brown waxed-cotton jacket, and brown leather boots, stands near Sarah, an adult woman with chin-length blonde hair, rectangular glasses, blue eyes, a purple blouse, grey skirt, yellow scarf, small grey drop earrings, and black boots, both smiling warmly as they look out over the balcony railing. Wide shot showing the grey concrete balcony floor, the white metal railing, the potted dark green shrub with russet leaves at the right, the open balcony door frame at the left with the white cardboard rocket resting inside the living room, and distant rooftops beneath the twilight sky.

